# Complete fix + verify (no half work)

User ne jo bug/feature bola hai, **end-to-end working** banana hai. “Code likh diya” kaafi nahi.

## Must

1. **Poora fix** — sirf ek layer mat chhodo (API theek, UI cache/stale; ya mock OK, DB skip). Public page, admin, save path, timeout, cache — jo user dekhega woh sab.
2. **Pehle cause, phir patch** — guess pe “ho gaya” mat bolo. File/path khol ke evidence lo.
3. **Bina check/test ke mat chhodo** — local verify: relevant page/API, empty/error path, jo pehle toot raha tha. UI change ho to browser ya curl. Test/e2e ho to chalao.
4. **Final working** — timeout, cache (`force-dynamic`), galat field (`publishedAt` vs `updatedAt`), mock-vs-DB, deploy ke bina live pe dikhega ya nahi — yeh soch ke band karo.
5. **Honest status** — half fix ho to “done” mat likho. Kya verify hua, kya nahi, seedha batao.
6. **400 lines** — source file 400 se upar mat rakho. Edit se 400 cross ho to pehle split, phir fix.

## Don't

- Adha patch + “fix ho gaya”
- Sirf repo function change, page cache/timeout ignore
- Bina run/check ke push/deploy ready claim

## Example

- ❌ News date: `publishedAt = now` repo me, 2s `tryPrisma` timeout + cached article page — live purani date.
- ✅ Same save DB pe persist, public date latest time, article route fresh, phir verify.
